    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d302">

                <pb facs="0441" n="347" sameAs="frus:frus1930v03/pg347"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.5048/284: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Liberia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Hall</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-06-18T11:00:00-00:44">June 18, 1930—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 4:59 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>86. Mass meeting was held yesterday by ex-President Howard, Chief Justice
                    Johnson, Gray,<anchor n="27" xml:id="d302-f1"/> and Faulkner and adopted
                    resolutions condemning the present administration for its part in the slave
                    trade and further that the people of Liberia desired the officials responsible
                    removed from office.</p>
                <p>[Paraphrase.] In spite of the Liberian Government’s determined opposition, the
                    meeting was held and there were about 200 persons in attendance. While it is
                    doubted that this meeting will have any direct effect, it does show the general
                    feeling of a large portion of the population. Despatch follows by pouch.<anchor
                        n="28" xml:id="d302-f2"/> [End paraphrase.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hall</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d302-f1" n="27" xml:id="d302-f1-content">
                <p>P. O. Gray, editor of the <hi rendition="#italic">Liberia Express and
                        Agricultural World</hi>.</p>
            </note>
